<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ja'alin</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Jaalin, Ja'aliyyin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ja'alin are an Arab tribe of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a> valley in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sudan">Sudan</a>, centred on the region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shendi">Shendi</a>, who claim descent from al-Abbas, the uncle of the Prophet. Many became merchants trading across Sudan in the 19th century. In 1822 their chief, Mek Nimr of Shendi, killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-kamil-pasha">Ismail Kamil Pasha</a>, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ali-of-egypt">Muhammad Ali of Egypt</a>, provoking savage reprisals by the Turco-Egyptian army.</p></div>
